es 24, where the end of the second series caught 19, with its controls 5 of 5. One test failed once in one run of fifty and was not seen again in three reruns; its cause is not known. MAIN'S WORD ON THE NINETEEN UNQUOTED ROWS OF THE REGISTRY OF RETRACTED PHRASES, which the seat asked for: its proposal as sent, the stricter option, seventeen swept and two held by name as readings; the registry's two notes rewritten, each keeping what it said; an old debt paid (P-154): the sweep reads 54 rows, 46 swept and 8 that take back a reading. MENDED BY MAIN AT THE LANDING: B1632's claim line leads with the correction it had carried at its end, and the row of the paper's page that showed its first words carries it; the seat's table of standing lines shortened by that line, to eleven; a test of B1890 whose name still said the gap was there renamed. 0 of 19. | yes | 3 |
